{{Quote | ''The field is abound with trees.''}}
[[File:BattleBgForest.png|thumb]]

Forest Field is one of the [[Field Effects]] present in Rejuvenation. It is classified as a Telluric field and can be found in [[Route 1]], [[Goldenwood Forest]], [[Sheridan Village]], [[Route 3]] (and nearby areas), [[Terajuma Jungle]], and [[Kakori Village]]. Notable battles involving this field include [[Zetta]]'s battle in Goldenwood Forest and [[Keta]]'s battle in Sheridan Village.

==General Effects==

* Grass-type moves → 1.5x boost.
** ''"The forestry strengthened the attack!"''
* Special Bug-type moves → 1.5x boost.
** ''"The attack spread throughout the forest!"''
* When overlayed, [[Grassy Terrain]] lasts 8 turns.

==Abilities Affected==

===Activated Abilities===

* Grass Pelt
* Leaf Guard
* Overgrow
* Swarm

===Buffed Abilities===

* Effect Spore's activation chance is doubled to 60%.
* Honey Gather will always find Honey. Yummers.
* [[Jungle Beat]] boosts the power of the Pokémon's sound-based moves by 50%.
** As of V14.0.22, this effect isn't listed in the in-game Field Notes.
* Sap Sipper restores 1/16 of the bearer's Max HP at the end of each turn.
** ''"[Pokémon] drank tree sap to recover!"''
* [[Wildfire]] inflicts 1/6 of the foes' Max HP as damage per turn.
** This damage isn't doubled if the target is burned, making it 1/6th regardless of status.
** As of V14.0.22, this effect isn't listed in the in-game Field Notes.

==Moves Affected==

===Damage Modifiers===

====Moves which receive an attack buff====

* Cut → 2x boost, Grass sub-typing.
** ''"A tree slammed down!"''
* Air Cutter, Air Slash, Breaking Swipe, Fury Cutter, [[Gale Strike]], Psycho Cut, Slash → 1.5x boost, Grass sub-typing.
** ''"A tree slammed down!"''
* Attack Order, Branch Poke, Electroweb, Grav Apple → 1.5x boost.
** ''"They're coming out of the woodwork!"''
** ''"Straight from the tree!"''
** ''"Gossamer and arbor strengthened the attack!"''
** ''"The apple did not fall far from the tree!"''

====Moves which receive an attack nerf====

* Muddy Water, Surf → 0.5x decrease.
** ''"The forest softened the attack..."''

===Other Moves===

====Buffed Moves====

* Chloroblast's recoil is 25% of the user's Max HP.
* Defend Order raises the user's Defense and Special Defense by 2 stages.
* Forest's Curse places a Curse on the target.
** ''"[Pokémon] put a curse on [Target]!"''
* Growth raises the user's Attack and Special Attack by 2 stages.
** This does not stack with this move's existing boost in Harsh Sunlight.
* Heal Order restores 66% of the user's max HP.
* Infestation inflicts 1/6 of the target's Max HP as damage per turn.
* Ingrain restores 1/8 of the user's Max HP at the end of each turn.
* Jungle Healing restores the HP of the user and its allies by 33% of their Max HP.
* Nature's Madness deals damage equal to 75% of the opponent's remaining HP.
* Silk Trap protects the user from status moves
* Sticky Web lowers affected Pokémon's Speed by 2 stages on switch-in.
* Strength Sap's recovery is increased by 30%.

===Field-dependent moves & Abilities===

* Mimicry changes the bearer's type to Bug.
* Camouflage changes the user's type to Bug.
* Nature Power becomes Wood Hammer.
* Secret Power may induce Sleep.
* Shelter halves damage from Bug-type moves.
* Terrain Pulse's type becomes Bug.

==Transitions to Other Fields==

'''Any move in this section inherently gains a 1.3x damage boost on top of any other previously listed modifiers.'''

* This field will transform into [[Swamp Field]] if Surf is used 3 times or Muddy Water is used 2 times.
** ''"The ground became waterlogged..."''
** ''"The forest became marshy!"''
*** Specifically, using Surf increments the counter by +1 and using Muddy Water increments it by +2. The field changes to Swamp Field when the counter reaches 3.

==Items==

* [[Telluric Seed]] applies Spiky Shield to the user.
** ''"The Telluric Seed shielded [Pokémon] against damage!"''

==Notes==

* As of V14.0.22, despite what the in-game Field Notes and the inspection screen say, Long Reach does not decrease the bearer's Accuracy on this field. This effect is exclusive to Pokémon Reborn.

